    "Reserved an extra 64-KiB gap before the journal after an updater EOF-boundary regression failed.",
    "Initialized changed-choice writes in indirect mode after the linked counter exposed a redundant status-register write.",
    "Changed button actions to presses after the menu-release regression launched the wrong image. Final manual lanes require no handoff before the explicit user action."
  ],
  "firmware_source_commit": "a41cecfa6247b00fcc96a113ba085bd8b02b0c50",
  "interpretation": [
    "Automatic runs include the stock loader baseline of one status-register write; the selector adds none.",
    "A changed choice programs one 80-byte journal record; recycling a full journal sector additionally erases one 4-KiB sector.",
    "Changed and recycled choices use two and four SDK status-register writes respectively. These are reported separately from array programming.",
    "Manual lanes start with independently observed loader QSPI/clock context. Automatic Dirt and FDN lanes execute the stock loader from reset.",
    "Handoffs verify exact payload bytes, reset PC, VTOR/MSP and a cleared DMA arena. RAM payloads stop at reset entry; Dirt reaches its main entry.",
    "The complete modeled NOR remains unchanged outside the two choice sectors."
  ],
